{
  "name": "mina",
  "description": "Mina is a succinct blockchain protocol that utilizes recursive Zero-Knowledge Succinct Non-interactive Arguments of Knowledge (zk-SNARKs) to maintain a constant-sized state. It leverages OCaml for the core protocol logic, incorporating advanced cryptographic primitives such as Kimchi and Plonk for recursive proof composition. The system is architected to support high-assurance decentralized applications (zkApps) while remaining verifiable by hardware with limited computational resources.",
